From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:19:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: macsmc: Report the thermal pressure level on the
 14-inch M4 MacBook Pro

The driver exposes the SMC thermal pressure level as
thermal_pressure_level when the machine has a readable si32 pressure key,
and takes the key from its board table when the device tree names none,
as for the M3 machines.

The J604's SMC key list (debugfs macsmc-hwmon/keys on 1.608) has mTPL
as a readable si32 (flags 0x85), the key the M3 entries use, and its
ADT names the same key for macOS: /arm-io/smctempsensor0 (compatible
"smc-tempsensor") has sensor = "mTPL" with a 1000 ms timerInterval. Add the
J604 with that pressure key only: the SoC die zone stays M3-only, and
this machine's die temperatures come from the PMP. A key that does not
read is ignored with a warning, so the worst case is no attribute.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
index 7852fe5270..2d3a74c46f 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
@@ -119,6 +119,16 @@ static const struct macsmc_hwmon_board {
 		.die_keys = "Tg0D,Tg0P,Tg0X,Tg0b,Tg0j,Tg0v,Te05,Te0P,Tp05,Tp0L,Tp0b,Tp0r",
 		.pressure_key = "mTPL",
 	},
+	/*
+	 * MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4): mTPL is a readable si32 in this
+	 * machine's key list, as on the M3 machines above. No die key list:
+	 * the SoC die zone is M3-only and this machine's die temperatures
+	 * come from the PMP.
+	 */
+	{
+		.compatible = "apple,j604",
+		.pressure_key = "mTPL",
+	},
 };
 
 static bool macsmc_hwmon_is_m3(void)
